# - Acast, Thank God It is Toby Highlights, episode Tehilah, Shout Radio (opened 2026-10-20, episode dated Thursday January 14, 2021): Tehilah (Kelsey Tehilah LeBlanc) is a breath of fresh air. With her new found Antillean Soul style of music, she meshes her West Indian roots with her modern soft toned vocals to produce an intimate, captivating listen. Introduced to singing by being involved in the church choir at a young age. Self taught guitarist. Performed at many festivals and quite a few intimate shows on her home island of The Commonwealth of Dominica. Her vision is to be a source of self care through her sound.
# - Qobuz, Reo discography page carrying the Music Story biography (search result and listing rechecked 2026-10-20): La vie doux, Reo feat. Tehilah, released by Reo music Ent. on 26 June 2025; the Music Story text states that at the end of 2025 Reo scored a chart hit with La vie doux, a duet with Tehilah that reached number 4 in the Outre-Mer Songs chart. The same biography gives Reo real name and Colihaut, Dominica origin, used here only as collaborator context already carried on this site Reo profile.
# - Caribbean Entertainment Hub, Lady Lava Leads With 9 Nominations In Caribbean Music Awards 4th Year (opened 2026-10-20, article dated June 10, 2026): Bouyon Song of the Year nominees list includes La Vie Doux by Reo & Tehilah, alongside Bouwey, Bye to the Old Me, Put That on That, Se Miimii, Shake Something, Take Me as I Am and Time 2 Grind. AntiMusic nominees announcement (search result, 2026-10-20) carries the same list.
# - Caribbean Music Awards 2026 winners lists (search results, 2026-10-20, faded4u, Kribbean, Ameyaw Debrah, Caribbean E Magazine): Bouyon Song of the Year winner was Bouwey by 1T1 & Theomaa, and Bouyon Artist of the Year was Mr. Ridge. La Vie Doux was therefore a nominee, not the winner.
# - YouTube, Bouyon Music 2026 Mix Vol. 1 by Bouyon Shattaz, mixed by Smokiller (search result, 2026-10-20): tracklist chapter at 37:02, Reo x Tehilah, La Vie Doux, inside a mix of new Dominica bouyon.
# - Homonyms separated, not claimed: Future Youth Records artist page for Tehillah (search result, 2026-10-20), a UK creative born and based in the South East of England, with the Still Here EP, a different spelling with a double l and a different biography; and Tehila of tehilamusic.com (search result, 2026-10-20), a singer songwriter whose family moved from Israel to Hawaii, a different name spelling and a different path. Neither is the Dominican Tehilah of La Vie Doux, and no record of theirs is claimed here.
# Note: only one recording is verified for the Dominican Tehilah in the sources consulted: La Vie Doux. No solo single, EP or album under her own name was verified, and no official artist account was verified by opening it, so sameAs stays empty. This is a THIN recording dossier with a documented biography, and the profile states both parts openly.

